{"name":"Valise","hex":"#80502b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"valise","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece of hand luggage such as a suitcase or travelling bag."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/valise"}],"entries":[{"title":"Suitcase","blocks":[{"text":"A suitcase is a form of baggage. It is a rectangular container with a handle and is typically used to carry one's clothes and other belongings while traveling. The first suitcases appeared in the late 19th century due to the increased popularity of mass tourism at the time, and were meant to hold dress suits. They were originally made using heavier materials such as leather or steel, but, beginning in the 1930s, were constructed with more lightweight materials like plastic and cardboard."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Suitcase1.jpg/330px-Suitcase1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suitcase"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Suitcase_%28AM_2001.25.958-6%29.jpg/500px-Suitcase_%28AM_2001.25.958-6%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Suitcase_%28AM_2001.25.958-6%29.jpg/1280px-Suitcase_%28AM_2001.25.958-6%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Suitcase_%28AM_2001.25.958-6%29.jpg/500px-Suitcase_%28AM_2001.25.958-6%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A brown leather suitcase from the Auckland War Memorial Museum that belonged to a QAIMNS staff nurse during World War I","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASuitcase_(AM_2001.25.958-6).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Rolling_luggage_patent_1.png/500px-Rolling_luggage_patent_1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Rolling_luggage_patent_1.png/1280px-Rolling_luggage_patent_1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Rolling_luggage_patent_1.png/500px-Rolling_luggage_patent_1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An illustration from Bernard D. Sadow's 1972 patent for rolling luggage","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARolling_luggage_patent_1.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Bluesmart_connected_carry-on_%2817135575321%29.jpg/500px-Bluesmart_connected_carry-on_%2817135575321%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Bluesmart_connected_carry-on_%2817135575321%29.jpg/1280px-Bluesmart_connected_carry-on_%2817135575321%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Bluesmart_connected_carry-on_%2817135575321%29.jpg/500px-Bluesmart_connected_carry-on_%2817135575321%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A smart suitcase created by Bluesmart, whose suitcases came with GPS tracking, an internal scale, and other features. The company shut down in 2018, which it blamed on a ban by many major airlines on smart suitcases with nonremovable lithium-ion batteries.[24]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABluesmart_connected_carry-on_(17135575321).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/%27Far_Out%27_Case.jpg/500px-%27Far_Out%27_Case.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/%27Far